{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous","id":1294000,"title":"Demons - must they be dangerous?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-05T05:00:51-08:00","id":1294000,"title":"Demons - must they be dangerous?","content":"OK. Demons. Must they be dangerous? <br /> <br /> I did a demon compilation:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/223770-homebrews-of-the-first-circle\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/223770-homebrews-of-the-first-circle\"> Homebrews of the First Circle? - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/223770-homebrews-of-the-first-circle\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/223770-homebrews-of-the-first-circle </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Something I was curious about. I've been looking, but I'm having trouble finding any Homebrew First Circles. I found two(both in a blog named Octipodial Preservation), but that's pretty much it for anything with stats. So, does anyone know where I can find some? Those which were on the Lost Wiki would be </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> A shitton of demons there are kinda benign. Or hassling. But very rare are dangerous.<br /> <br /> I just got from this thread:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/252535-demonology-and-morality/page16\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/252535-demonology-and-morality/page16\"> Demonology And Morality - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/252535-demonology-and-morality/page16\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/252535-demonology-and-morality/page16 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> So on the rpg.net thread the topic came up of celestial circle demon summoning. Basically a second circle demon is supposed to be a pretty damn big deal, to the point where it might seem too powerful for the XP cost ect. That was countered by StephenLS basically saying that performing blood rituals at the </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> OK. Question. <br /> <br /> Must demons be dangerous? Must a demon, by its very presence, be inimical to mortal society?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T05:04:23-08:00","id":1294002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous#post1294000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK. Demons. Must they be dangerous?<br /> <br /> I did a demon compilation:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/223770-homebrews-of-the-first-circle\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/223770-homebrews-of-the-first-circle\"> Homebrews of the First Circle? - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/223770-homebrews-of-the-first-circle\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/223770-homebrews-of-the-first-circle </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Something I was curious about. I've been looking, but I'm having trouble finding any Homebrew First Circles. I found two(both in a blog named Octipodial Preservation), but that's pretty much it for anything with stats. So, does anyone know where I can find some? Those which were on the Lost Wiki would be </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> A shitton of demons there are kinda benign. Or hassling. But very rare are dangerous.<br /> <br /> I just got from this thread:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/252535-demonology-and-morality/page16\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/252535-demonology-and-morality/page16\"> Demonology And Morality - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/252535-demonology-and-morality/page16\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/252535-demonology-and-morality/page16 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> So on the rpg.net thread the topic came up of celestial circle demon summoning. Basically a second circle demon is supposed to be a pretty damn big deal, to the point where it might seem too powerful for the XP cost ect. That was countered by StephenLS basically saying that performing blood rituals at the </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> OK. Question.<br /> <br /> Must demons be dangerous? Must a demon, by its very presence, be inimical to mortal society?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think they necessarily need to be <i>dangerous</i> per se, but they do have to be... strange, odd, alien and/or disquieting. Neomah, for instance, aren't precisely <i>dangerous</i> natively (any more than a strong human is; they're not bad combatants) but the way that they create life without regard to what that life will do will inevitably lead to issues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T05:06:27-08:00","id":1294004,"title":"","content":"My understanding is that demons are dangerous, effectively, due to extreme values dissonance; i.e., Malfean civilization runs on and inculcates values that, yes, are intrinsically inimical to mortal ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T05:06:52-08:00","id":1294005,"title":"","content":"Not really. Demons are always alien, but as far back as Games of Divinity we had the Sesseljae and Angyalkae, both of whom are relatively harmless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T05:18:53-08:00","id":1294008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1294005#post1294005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really. Demons are always alien, but as far back as Games of Divinity we had the Sesseljae and Angyalkae, both of whom are relatively harmless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um... No. <br /> <br /> Sesseljae and Angyalkae can most definitely be disruptive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T05:29:19-08:00","id":1294010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1294008#post1294008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Um... No.<br /> <br /> Sesseljae and Angyalkae can most definitely be disruptive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Disruptive != Dangerous<br /> <br /> A Sesselja isn't going to be harming people by default (places that serve intoxicants are in danger, I suppose, but unless they serve a medicinal use the stomach bottle bug isn't going to do more than consume stock and make unhappy customers), and while an Angyalka may cause some uncomfortable personal insights, they aren't particularly aggressive, either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T06:01:21-08:00","id":1294016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous#post1294000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Must demons be dangerous?</div> </div> </div> </div>Who said they must be?<br /> <br /> Hell, half the demons that actually are dangerous don't need to be, so long as they're carefully managed; don't summon more hopping puppeteers than you can keep an eye on, and keep people from getting a taste of their mucus, and you should be able to avoid tragedy.<br /> <br /> First Circle Demons don't need to be dangerous, but they should be a bit monomaniacal. Not just capable of an unusual thing, but fixated on it to a point where they'll cause a stir if left to their own devices.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T06:06:29-08:00","id":1294017,"title":"","content":"OK.<br /> <br /> Sesseljae consume poisons. <br /> <br /> They die. <br /> <br /> Two more are born. These aren't bound. What happens next? A veritable plague. No more alcohol. No more drugs. No more medicine. No more painkillers. And these... Insects are jumping in and out of people's bodies. <br /> <br /> That's disruptive. <br /> <br /> And angyalkae... 13 dice. Greatest possible mortal skill, with charms added. And it is played nonstop. Yes, there will be suicide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T07:01:46-08:00","id":1294030,"title":"","content":"This isn't accurate. They reproduce in the demon city by swarming to consume something especially poisonous, but not every one of them that dies of poison singularly, anywhere in existence, necessarily splits into two unbound demons.<br /> <br /> Also, even in 2e, social influence couldn't drive you to suicide, nor were angyalkae particularly prone to try and cause such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 03-05-2019, 10:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T07:02:00-08:00","id":1294031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1294017#post1294017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK.<br /> <br /> Sesseljae consume poisons.<br /> <br /> They die.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes they die. Sesseljae in both prior Editions were given excellent Resistance. In the descriptive text, sesslejae dying en masse is attributed to them encountering substances sufficient to cause discomfort to the Yozis.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two more are born. These aren't bound.</div> </div> </div> </div>What are you basing this on? Neither previous write-up described either of these eventualities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens next? A veritable plague.</div> </div> </div> </div>Jesus Christ, how much poison was there in this town?! Maybe it deserves to be overrun by stomach bottle bugs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">No more painkillers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably no painkillers from the start...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And these... Insects are jumping in and out of people's bodies.<br /> <br /> That's disruptive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, for one thing, if there's no more alcohol, why are the demons jumping in and out of people's bodies? They primarily do that to get at alcohol.<br /> <br /> Second, sure, if the event that you're describing happened, it would be disruptive.<br /> <br /> Unless anybody has any salt. Some salt will make them go away. Surrounding them in a circle of it will make them very reluctant to go anywhere else.<br /> <br /> Would you make the Occult roll to figure that out very high difficulty? I wouldn't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And angyalkae... 13 dice. Greatest possible mortal skill, with charms added. And it is played nonstop. Yes, there will be suicide.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, that escalated quickly. What was up with these people's lives that being exposed to the music that gives them the measure of it results in suicide?<br /> <br /> Because in a world like most of Creation, which probably doesn't have the best emotional support systems, that was probably going to end up happening in those cases anyway. Maybe spread out a bit more, but still perhaps comparatively uncommon.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T07:39:44-08:00","id":1294047,"title":"","content":"As far as I see it demons have two major issues with integrating into human society.<br /> <br /> -Spirits in general are a little like neurodivergent people who were born with superpowers, which gives them much less incentive to examine their behaviours and rein in their worst impulses.<br /> -Living in Malfeas is going to make a lot of demons pretty maladjusted. Most First Circle demons don\u2019t know what it means to have rights as an individual and associate vulnerability with death. A Neomah sets herself up as an exotic courtesan; can she handle being confronted by a jealous spouse?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T08:00:50-08:00","id":1294055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1294047#post1294047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Neomah sets herself up as an exotic courtesan; can she handle being confronted by a jealous spouse?</div> </div> </div> </div>Is the neomah trying to pass themselves off as human?<br /> <br /> I wonder how jealous pre-existing relationships intersect with the rule of thumb &quot;assume it's a god and call a priest&quot;.<br /> <br /> (Note that my basis for making the roll to figure that salt will ward off an overenthusiastic sesseljae not being hard would be the world having a general rule of &quot;when in doubt, throw salt at it&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T08:47:37-08:00","id":1294070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1294055#post1294055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the neomah trying to pass themselves off as human?</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, the premise is that she's trying to integrate into human society. A Neomah's general apperance isn't exactly outside Creation's broad range of what can be considered human even if she's not exactly lying about what she is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T11:21:33-08:00","id":1294114,"title":"","content":"There probably are a few demons who you wouldn't mind having as neighbors (as long as you don't mind your neighbors being a bit eccentric), but there are no demons who could be mistaken for normal, well-adjusted members of human society. They're all <i>weird</i>, but some of them are weird in ways that aren't likely to hurt you.<br /> <br /> A demon trying to fully integrate into human society would probably run into a lot of awkward misunderstandings, but some of them could manage. A neomah could probably do it if someone who understands both mortal and Malfean culture made an effort to explain things to her.<br /> <br /> If sufficiently powerful humans can adapt to living in Hell (e.g. Gemstone Ocean Hero), some demons can surely adapt to living among humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T12:34:23-08:00","id":1294133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1294114#post1294114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A neomah could probably do it if someone who understands both mortal and Malfean culture made an effort to explain things to her.<br /> <br /> If sufficiently powerful humans can adapt to living in Hell (e.g. Gemstone Ocean Hero), some demons can surely adapt to living among humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know. Unless they changed demons, they can't really adapt. Your neomah could be made to understand certain rules of living in Creation, but never understand why the rules exist. It would be like living next to a sociopath, they only follow rules because they don't like the penalty, not because they understand why the rules are what they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24266-aoi-cobalt","name":"Aoi Cobalt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T13:35:51-08:00","id":1294157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aoi Cobalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1294133#post1294133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know. Unless they changed demons, they can't really adapt. Your neomah could be made to understand certain rules of living in Creation, but never understand why the rules exist. It would be like living next to a sociopath, they only follow rules because they don't like the penalty, not because they understand why the rules are what they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe. But there are sociopaths who function in society without doing anything all that bad, aren't there? If they follow the rules, does it really matter if they understand why the rules exist?<br /> <br /> Of course, most mortal societies wouldn't want a neomah repeatedly creating and abandoning bizarre hybrid children -- but some neomah have different passions. And a neomah could probably come to understand how being a valued member of a human community is a lot safer than living in Malfeas (leaving her free to pursue whatever arts she desires), even if she doesn't really understand all the mortals' bizarre hang-ups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T13:44:19-08:00","id":1294162,"title":"","content":"Isn't this what exorcists and shamans and stuff are for? In the world of Exalted there are strange spiritual beings who are hard to work with and often dangerous if you don't know what you're doing, or what you're dealing with.<br /> <br /> #ProtectShamanJobs","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T14:07:11-08:00","id":1294166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aoi Cobalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1294133#post1294133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know. Unless they changed demons, they can't really adapt. Your neomah could be made to understand certain rules of living in Creation, but never understand why the rules exist. It would be like living next to a sociopath, they only follow rules because they don't like the penalty, not because they understand why the rules are what they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Look just because they don't think like us doesn't mean a demon can't WANT to try. They'd probably be seen as odd by demons for wanting to live with people, and people would probably see them as odd for being a demon, but there's no reason why some odd demons may want to try to understand people.<br /> <br /> And like, going back to the Neomah example... I imagine that say, a hypothetical unbound Neomah could settle near a village, and gain a level of respect from the outsiders who beseech the Neomah for a child. The Neomah has no personal fondness for the formed baby, since it prefers the Baby-Forging more than the results, but they pass the child off to the ones who beseech them. The people of the village see this Neomah as perhaps strange, but one who has given children to those who want them for generations. And the Neomah gets to make children without doing any Sexy Stuff, which the writeup seemed to imply being a service they perform solely to feed their enjoyment of Baby-Smithing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T14:09:02-08:00","id":1294170,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, I just realized that maybe I should elaborate. So electricity is dangerous, if enough current is available and voltage present to drive it through your body it can do all kinds of bad things. It can bloat your muscles, stop your heart, cook you inside out. It can also cause shorts if improperly installed or nibbled on by rodents, and that can damage electrical equipment, start fires, and do all kinds of things. Fire is another thing that's actually pretty dangerous, even.<br /> <br /> That's why we have electricians who's job is to do that kind of thing. Now, they aren't gods, they can't just make anything safe, or make anything do anything. They're bound by the rules of the electricity that they deal with. You can't just energize the housing of an ungrounded toaster and call it safe because an electrician did it. So try to think of demonologists the same way. No, hopping puppeteers aren't safe, but they're damned good construction workers, if memory serves. Use them appropriately, observe the Occult Safety and Health Administration guildlines, and be constantly vigilant and you should be okay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T15:21:17-08:00","id":1294186,"title":"","content":"The main vice I imagine in most First Circle Demons that aren't outright mindless is a lack of patience. I picture trying to teach blood apes to operate a siege engine might result in them making a game attempt at the start, but in not much time they'd get bored and frustrated and just tear the machine apart.<br /> <br /> I see something different in demons whose drive is not extreme, and some capacity for empathy can derive from it.<br /> <br /> Neomah have an innate capacity to know what appeals to others sexually and emotionally. I'd say that's a place to start.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T15:38:38-08:00","id":1294190,"title":"","content":"I wonder how much mileage you\u2019d get out of considering demons to be more like relatively loyal slaves, rather than what most people seem to treat them as almost advanced AIs. Like I\u2019ve seen people say as long as you word your task binding with enough precision or word instructions well enough when directing them then you\u2019re fine. Like you could have a puppeteer as a babysitter as long as you magically bind them in an ironclad contract.<br /> <br /> It might be better to say that a puppeteer babysitter won\u2019t do anything bad as long as Master is close by keeping a watch, but left to its own devices it\u2019s more prone to fall to its own weaknesses. It might be really conflicted about doing it, it knows it shouldn\u2019t and it doesn\u2019t want to disappoint you, but surely just a little cuddle...it looks so cold....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T15:52:53-08:00","id":1294197,"title":"","content":"Like, the system models sorcerous binding as an Intimacy, so apart from the matter of how it can't be changed, it should be treated like an Intimacy; they won't follow it any more maniacally than they'd be inclined to for any other, and other Intimacies of Defining level might be given priority.<br /> <br /> For hopping puppeteers in particular, the way they were always described in prior Editions made them extremely restless and widespread, and liable to extreme frustration with giving them something too confining to do. Heck, if you went by the deeper demon binding rules of Second Edition, task binding a demon really specifically was liable to cause it to build up Limit very rapidly, and when it Broke, the degree to which the binding restrained it would slip a bit.<br /> <br /> That being said, I think that trying to be extremely intricate with a task binding is not really in the spirit of things, and being a clever bollocks besides. I actually think that the Intimacy modelling is another thing that would help out there; if it's something way more verbose and multi-faceted than you would actually expect somebody to have as a Principle, you can't bind a demon to it.<br /> <br /> And again, hopping puppeteers... they're fairly mindless, and those legs just unfurl in every direction, twining around all sorts. They read to me as likely to snare up the little bodies of babies without even being fully conscious of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T16:41:40-08:00","id":1294216,"title":"","content":"In other words, the greatest danger is the holdovers from life in the demon city, and their own native power?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T16:54:03-08:00","id":1294226,"title":"","content":"What I keep in mind when making demons is they often will represent nervosa of the Primordials soul hierarchy. Angyallka are rather pleasant and calm, but then again they don\u2019t seem to be able to do anything besides play music, and maybe some consort type stuff, but they are representative of primordial who like many of her kind was solipsistic, and had a hard time interacting with others in a way that wasn\u2019t murder, and Angyallka are atavisms from before the Primordials Became Yozis.<br /> <br /> Now all the Yozis are kept in a cage too small and all their madness is festering and bumping into each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T16:58:26-08:00","id":1294229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aoi Cobalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1294133#post1294133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know. Unless they changed demons, they can't really adapt. Your neomah could be made to understand certain rules of living in Creation, but never understand why the rules exist. It would be like living next to a sociopath, they only follow rules because they don't like the penalty, not because they understand why the rules are what they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is fine, it works with Gods, Elementals and Raksha after all. A sociopath following at least the letter of the law is more then most can hope for with supernatural entities without coaching. And Solars have supernatural coaching, they can teach Brain Damages people how to read and perform surgery, if they were so inclined they could rewire a domesticated demon, and that before they use Sorcery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T17:29:13-08:00","id":1294245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous#post1294000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Must demons be dangerous? Must a demon, by its very presence, be inimical to mortal society?</div> </div> </div> </div>Must an exotic beast or person from an alien culture be? They don't <b>have </b>to be inimical or dangerous, but can be either or both depending on circunstances - sometimes too easily for the careless or ignorant. Same principle applies with 1st circle demons, with the &quot;bonus&quot; of powers to match your basic unruly spirit.<br /> <br /> And dealing with 2nd or 3rd circles ones ups the scale of complication, as their desires, egos, motivations and powers can easily rival those of high level deities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-16-2020, 02:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T18:17:02-08:00","id":1294268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1294216#post1294216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In other words, the greatest danger is the holdovers from life in the demon city, and their own native power?</div> </div> </div> </div>A teakettle courtier does not go ballistic at the sound of laughter because it is a behaviour instilled by how it lived at home, nor is it really an application of its power (although it does bestow the power to summon venomous creatures to assault the source of the offence); it's just the nature of that demon. A little fragment of the alien designs of the Yozis, filtered down through the local needs and preferences of the Second Circle Demons.<br /> <br /> Something like a violent trigger is not comprehensive, although a certain violence or transgression might play itself out mildly in a demon, filtered through other aspects of its nature; the true purpose and being of neomah is as a courtesan, but they realise the reproductive potential inherent to that indulgence through moulding flesh (possibly acquired from a direct, if not quite painful) extraction, into an odd little baby that they carelessly abandon.<br /> <br /> Although one could see a bit more direct violence in being a courtesan that can spit fire, but that's beside the point<br /> <br /> For the ones that are dangerous, it's just their intrinsic behaviour, whether it's endemic to their actions or a response to some obscure activity. As being summoned by sorcerers goes, the former is something it's likely to try and squeeze in in addition to fulfilling your commands, and the latter is something that the demon likely often can't control itself with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T11:45:25-08:00","id":1294463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aoi Cobalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1294133#post1294133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your neomah could be made to understand certain rules of living in Creation, but never understand why the rules exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's normal for ANYONE who's lived under Cecelyne's legal code. The important element here isn't understanding why the rules are what they are; it's abiding by them. It's up to society to set the guidelines necessary for the safety of its individual participants. The demon might have to do some adapting, but society would as well... which is normal, society adapts to changing circumstances CONSTANTLY.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11867-caffeine-delusions","name":"Caffeine Delusions","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11867_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T20:54:31-08:00","id":1294582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caffeine Delusions</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1294463#post1294463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's normal for ANYONE who's lived under Cecelyne's legal code. The important element here isn't understanding why the rules are what they are; it's abiding by them. It's up to society to set the guidelines necessary for the safety of its individual participants. The demon might have to do some adapting, but society would as well... which is normal, society adapts to changing circumstances CONSTANTLY.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's also the old point of the demon getting the idea, but getting the reason wrong. 2nd edition Malfean law amounted to the strong are free to do what they want with those weaker, so long as it doesn't become a problem for those even stronger than the first group. So a demon given the laws of the village they want to move into might get the rules read and instead of going, &quot;Ah these are the rules set forth to minimize discomfort, distrust, irritation, and such to give the best odds of survival and contentment for the group.&quot; no they grew up in the Malfeas they know the score really works like this, &quot;So these are the rules the most powerful want obeyed as they cause the least inconveniance and disruption to their own works and desires and failure to follow said rules means you better be sure you can overthrow those powers or you are screwed.&quot; *<br /> <br /> *Also no one in town gets why said demon refuses to look at the sky and has been known to scream and slam doors in your face if you show up wearing the wrong shade of blue, but that's just weird demon stuff. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T22:12:59-08:00","id":1294606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1294114#post1294114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If sufficiently powerful humans can adapt to living in Hell (e.g. Gemstone Ocean Hero), some demons can surely adapt to living among humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think individuals can adapt. I think the issue is that many wouldn't necessarily want to adapt to an alien environment, where they're hated, feared and usually live as slaves. In contrast, would you want to adapt to a life in hell on such terms?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24366-slarn","name":"Slarn!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24366_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T22:36:57-08:00","id":1294611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1294031#post1294031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jesus Christ, how much poison was there in this town?! Maybe it deserves to be overrun by stomach bottle bugs.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;I'm telling you, Jyethryo, this place has been going downhill ever since the bugs arrived. First the poison mine was overrun, then local lake of poison got drained, and now they've shut down Poison Anne's Poisoned Teahouse. It's getting to the point where a man can't find a good mug of poison in this town. Poisonville just ain't what it once was.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T04:21:23-08:00","id":1294673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1294611#post1294611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;I'm telling you, Jyethryo, this place has been going downhill ever since the bugs arrived. First the poison mine was overrun, then local lake of poison got drained, and now they've shut down Poison Anne's Poisoned Teahouse. It's getting to the point where a man can't find a good mug of poison in this town. Poisonville just ain't what it once was.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Fine fine fine I get it. <br /> <br /> No sesseljae dying unless something drastic happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T05:31:03-08:00","id":1294684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1294673#post1294673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fine fine fine I get it. <br /> <br /> No sesseljae dying unless something drastic happens.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not what any of us said. Sesseljae die just fine, but they're better than most mortals are at resisting poison, and even dying of poison isn't what causes them to reproduce - they do so when they <i>mass together</i> and eat something toxic enough to be troublesome <i>to the Yozis</i>. That probably doesn't occur often in Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T05:36:04-08:00","id":1294688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1294684#post1294684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not what any of us said. Sesseljae die just fine, but they're better than most mortals are at resisting poison, and even dying of poison isn't what causes them to reproduce - they do so when they <i>mass together</i> and eat something toxic enough to be troublesome <i>to the Yozis</i>. That probably doesn't occur often in Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what i meant by 'something drastic happen'. <br /> <br /> I kinda thought that Sesseljae had toxins build up, and when they eat enough, their systems finally get over come and they die and they reproduce.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T05:46:25-08:00","id":1294691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1294688#post1294688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kinda thought that Sesseljae had toxins build up, and when they eat enough, their systems finally get over come and they die and they reproduce.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really, given how that write-up describes the sesseljae as needing to go through multiple cycles of consumption and death before they get to the point that the remains have processed the toxins out completely, I get the impression that any such scenario is actually resulting in a net loss of them.<br /> <br /> I'm not seeing it as their process of reproduction so much as them being able to at least salvage a situation when their intended purpose kills them en masse.<br /> <br /> But even if it was the case of &quot;any time their consumption of toxins kills them, two more sprout up&quot;, and even if one presumes that a summoned bug is already reaching the limit of its poison saturation, the point of my prior quip was that your proposed scenario only sounds like it happens once or twice before everything sufficiently toxic is used up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T05:57:57-08:00","id":1294696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1294691#post1294691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really, given how that write-up describes the sesseljae as needing to go through multiple cycles of consumption and death before they get to the point that the remains have processed the toxins out completely, I get the impression that any such scenario is actually resulting in a net loss of them.<br /> <br /> I'm not seeing it as their process of reproduction so much as them being able to at least salvage a situation when their intended purpose kills them en masse.<br /> <br /> But even if it was the case of &quot;any time their consumption of toxins kills them, two more sprout up&quot;, and even if one presumes that a summoned bug is already reaching the limit of its poison saturation, the point of my prior quip was that your proposed scenario only sounds like it happens once or twice before everything sufficiently toxic is used up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok. <br /> <br /> Anyway... now ending the derail. Thanks for the help. I guess its... ok, <br /> <br /> I suppose that the homebrew in the thread are ok, then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T06:11:03-08:00","id":1294702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1294696#post1294696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose that the homebrew in the thread are ok, then.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't recall any of us saying anything about homebrew, good or bad, save when you reposted my demon without my permission.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 03-07-2019, 09:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T06:19:03-08:00","id":1294705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1294702#post1294702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't recall any of us saying anything about homebrew, good or bad, save when you reposted my demon without my permission.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, sorry about that. <br /> <br /> The Homebrew was when I realized the majority of the demons I collected could, with a bit of effort, work in Creation just fine. A pastry smith can easily get along with a village, or a Gilldemperu can work in a noble house as a chef.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T06:31:14-08:00","id":1294715,"title":"","content":"I've mostly not read your demonic homebrew, since other times I've questioned your ideas, you've either jumped down my throat about it, or posted something like &quot;Sigh, fine,&quot; et cetera. <br /> <br /> I have no opinions about your demons, because I haven't read them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T07:25:49-08:00","id":1294729,"title":"","content":"I'm glad everyone seems to understand my reference. Demons aren't inherently evil, but they just don't fit into human culture. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caffeine Delusions</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1294463#post1294463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The demon might have to do some adapting, but society would as well... which is normal, society adapts to changing circumstances CONSTANTLY.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's the sticking point. Demons, and their masters, don't have the capability to adapt. They can't change what they are. Unlike the Raksha, demons are what they were created to be. A demon might obey a set of rules to exist in Creation, but they always will remain a demon. I think its their flaw, they are what they are. You can give a blood ape orders not to eat people or magically mess with its mind, but you can never convince one of its own will not to eat people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24266-aoi-cobalt","name":"Aoi Cobalt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T09:51:29-08:00","id":1294775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aoi Cobalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1294729#post1294729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm glad everyone seems to understand my reference. Demons aren't inherently evil, but they just don't fit into human culture.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think that's the sticking point. Demons, and their masters, don't have the capability to adapt. They can't change what they are. Unlike the Raksha, demons are what they were created to be. A demon might obey a set of rules to exist in Creation, but they always will remain a demon. I think its their flaw, they are what they are. You can give a blood ape orders not to eat people or magically mess with its mind, but you can never convince one of its own will not to eat people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure you can, they just need a steady supply of cats. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T10:20:06-08:00","id":1294786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aoi Cobalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1294729#post1294729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">they just don't fit into human culture.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which human culture; there are lots of them.<br /> <br /> Even a blood ape might fit in with something like, say, a mercenary army. Not every blood ape, but the kind that has a higher sense of camaraderie and sees better opportunities for violence and feeding by serving a specialised function within a fighting group.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aoi Cobalt</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demons, and their masters, don't have the capability to adapt. They can't change what they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this should apply to the extent that it makes them interesting. On the one side, deeply rooted compulsions and triggers make them a slightly tense thing for a sorcerer to employ, making that aspect of magic more than just having purpose-built automatons that look weird, and reinforcing the value of things like demonology manuals. On the other, I think one wants a bit of variety in characterisation for purposes of portrayal and interaction in a function besides summoning.<br /> <br /> Besides, both prior Editions have had the idea that there are First Circle Demons who can grow strong enough to qualify as citizens. I imagine that often comes with some more... refinement in the personality.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T13:57:29-08:00","id":1294874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this should apply to the extent that it makes them interesting. On the one side, deeply rooted compulsions and triggers make them a slightly tense thing for a sorcerer to employ, making that aspect of magic more than just having purpose-built automatons that look weird, and reinforcing the value of things like demonology manuals. On the other, I think one wants a bit of variety in characterisation for purposes of portrayal and interaction in a function besides summoning.<br /> <br /> Besides, both prior Editions have had the idea that there are First Circle Demons who can grow strong enough to qualify as citizens. I imagine that often comes with some more... refinement in the personality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I agree that demons, even 1st circle, are not automatons. They all have personalities and quirks. But their primary motivation, their defining intimacy is locked.<br /> Even the mercenary blood ape is going to want to commit mayhem and murder between jobs instead of getting drunk and such like his human mercenary buddies. The blood ape wants to commit the mayhem because it is what he does, getting wasted with his buddies never occurs to him.<br /> <br /> The blood ape could restrain itself, and not go off on a rampage, that's just an interesting story idea.<br /> But our blood ape could never decide to become a tailor or sell flowers, because his defining intimacy is to commit mayhem, and he can not change that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24266,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24266-aoi-cobalt","user":"Aoi Cobalt","date":". 03-07-2019, 05:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24266-aoi-cobalt","name":"Aoi Cobalt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T18:28:14-08:00","id":1294941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aoi Cobalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1294874#post1294874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The blood ape wants to commit the mayhem because it is what he does, getting wasted with his buddies never occurs to him.</div> </div> </div> </div>The barkeeps of the Demon City sure seem to work hard to keep their stores of alcohol safe from swarms of sesseljae; one would think that they wouldn't bother storing such substances if it wasn't profitable, if demons didn't at least<i> occasionally</i> want to come in and pay to drink it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T01:04:58-08:00","id":1294993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1294941#post1294941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The barkeeps of the Demon City sure seem to work hard to keep their stores of alcohol safe from swarms of sesseljae; one would think that they wouldn't bother storing such substances if it wasn't profitable, if demons didn't at least<i> occasionally</i> want to come in and pay to drink it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Demon City wouldn't exactly deserve to be called a city if it couldn't sustain a night-life. That's a town at best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11867-caffeine-delusions","name":"Caffeine Delusions","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11867_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T03:45:02-08:00","id":1295005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aoi Cobalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1294874#post1294874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I agree that demons, even 1st circle, are not automatons. They all have personalities and quirks. But their primary motivation, their defining intimacy is locked.<br /> Even the mercenary blood ape is going to want to commit mayhem and murder between jobs instead of getting drunk and such like his human mercenary buddies. The blood ape wants to commit the mayhem because it is what he does, getting wasted with his buddies never occurs to him.<br /> <br /> The blood ape could restrain itself, and not go off on a rampage, that's just an interesting story idea.<br /> But our blood ape could never decide to become a tailor or sell flowers, because his defining intimacy is to commit mayhem, and he can not change that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't know why you would raise the possibility of a blood ape deciding to become a florist only to dismiss it, that sounds like an amazing npc.<br /> <br /> More seriously I think the demons are much more interesting when they have the capacity for meaningful change, growth and individuality. One of the themes of exalted is that when you create things to do your will they will often grow out of your control, and demons should be no different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3174-carl-ollivier","name":"Carl.ollivier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T05:25:17-08:00","id":1295016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Carl.ollivier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1295005#post1295005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't know why you would raise the possibility of a blood ape deciding to become a florist only to dismiss it, that sounds like an amazing npc.<br /> <br /> More seriously I think the demons are much more interesting when they have the capacity for meaningful change, growth and individuality. One of the themes of exalted is that when you create things to do your will they will often grow out of your control, and demons should be no different.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suggest that because the creators of the original Exalted suggested it, that demons lacked the capacity for growth. Which is why they were demons. Which is why demons were never a playable concept, unlike every other power group. Which is why Infernals existed, because demons were not a playable group.<br /> It's the demon's flaw, and why they are only tools. It's why the Primordials can't escape their prison, because they can't change what they are to become something different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24266-aoi-cobalt","name":"Aoi Cobalt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T05:32:47-08:00","id":1295018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1294941#post1294941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The barkeeps of the Demon City sure seem to work hard to keep their stores of alcohol safe from swarms of sesseljae; one would think that they wouldn't bother storing such substances if it wasn't profitable, if demons didn't at least<i> occasionally</i> want to come in and pay to drink it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think 2nd and 3rd circle demons have tastes for alcohol. I don't know of many 1st circle demons that might. But maybe demons do drink. That isn't all our human mercenaries are doing (self edited for cleanlyness). I don't think our blood ape merc is going to join them in all their activities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24266-aoi-cobalt","name":"Aoi Cobalt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T05:42:52-08:00","id":1295021,"title":"","content":"With the exception of some support for playing gods and elementals in RoGD1 (and even that was more of an omission due to demons being in a different book than a deliberate statement on the nature of demons), I don't recall demons being particularly singled out as lacking the capability for growth.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T05:49:59-08:00","id":1295024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aoi Cobalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1295018#post1295018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think 2nd and 3rd circle demons have tastes for alcohol.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you feel that a business exclusively catering to <i>only</i> the greatest movers and shakers of Hell would function as anything resembling a bar? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aoi Cobalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1295018#post1295018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know of many 1st circle demons that might.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any demon intelligent enough to open a tab, realistically. People with stresses and anxiety in their lives often find their way to the bottle, and first circle demons are pretty thoroughly surrounded by stress and anxiety.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aoi Cobalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1295018#post1295018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think our blood ape merc is going to join them in all their activities.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't <i>have</i> to join in <i>all</i> their activities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T06:06:43-08:00","id":1295028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hug Ninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1295021#post1295021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the exception of some support for playing gods and elementals in RoGD1 (and even that was more of an omission due to demons being in a different book than a deliberate statement on the nature of demons), I don't recall demons being particularly singled out as lacking the capability for growth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it was in the writer's quotes and comments where they pointed this out. <br /> Not in a published work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24266-aoi-cobalt","name":"Aoi Cobalt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T06:18:33-08:00","id":1295031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1295024#post1295024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They don't <i>have</i> to join in <i>all</i> their activities.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the difference isn't they don't <i>have</i> to join in, because some humans also will choose not to join in.<br /> It's that they <i>can't</i> join in.<br /> <br /> And really, do you see a drunk blood ape as maintaining his control enough to not end up reverting to type and breaking those stupid human rules that it obeys only because it gives him a better chance to commit mayhem? Even humans fail that trick, and we usually understand why the rules exist.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24266-aoi-cobalt","name":"Aoi Cobalt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T06:24:51-08:00","id":1295034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1295024#post1295024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you feel that a business exclusively catering to <i>only</i> the greatest movers and shakers of Hell would function as anything resembling a bar?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. I've been in some very posh bars.<br /> Do you feel that a bar must be a grimy dive?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24266-aoi-cobalt","name":"Aoi Cobalt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T06:28:26-08:00","id":1295035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aoi Cobalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1295028#post1295028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it was in the writer's quotes and comments where they pointed this out.<br /> Not in a published work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean if it goes back far enough it has zero impact on my view of the setting because Infernals and Lunars weren't originally intended to be playable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T06:36:48-08:00","id":1295038,"title":"","content":"Look. Malfeas compass said there was demon ale in hell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T06:48:13-08:00","id":1295040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hug Ninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1295035#post1295035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean if it goes back far enough it has zero impact on my view of the setting because Infernals and Lunars weren't originally intended to be playable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know how far back it goes, but Infernals and Lunars were made playable.<br /> And part of making Infernals playable, they had to break their own rules to the setting so that Infernals could do what could never be done. And as part of that, they explained why it originally could not be done. Primordials and their demons literally could not change themselves. They are what they were, or what they were built to be (1st circle all were created for some purpose or reason). <br /> <br /> You want demons to become other things, go ahead, it's your game. I find it's more interesting that demons are demons because they lack the capacity to change, tragically they will always be tools and never the protagonist.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24266-aoi-cobalt","name":"Aoi Cobalt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T11:39:40-08:00","id":1295093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Carl.ollivier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1295005#post1295005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know why you would raise the possibility of a blood ape deciding to become a florist only to dismiss it, that sounds like an amazing npc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Especially the part where it takes payment in cats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T16:59:03-08:00","id":1295154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aoi Cobalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1295034#post1295034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. I've been in some very posh bars.</div> </div> </div> </div>I take it you're not secretly a queen or emperor or something? If you're not, then the fact that you've been in them at all makes it not the equivalent of a bar that only caters to second and third circles. We're talking a bar where rather than card you, they expect to see your face on the money when you pay. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aoi Cobalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1295034#post1295034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you feel that a bar must be a grimy dive?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but I'm absolutely certain the Demon City has far more grimy dives to keep the serfs pacified with alcohol, than it has posh bars that <i>only</i> serve Citizens and Unquestionable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T17:20:08-08:00","id":1295160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hug Ninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1295035#post1295035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean if it goes back far enough it has zero impact on my view of the setting because Infernals and Lunars weren't originally intended to be playable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have my doubts about that though, at least by the time the first ed corebook was published I highly doubt they never would have thought the Lunars were going to be given any sort of character creation rules, unless they thought Exalted was a one book Gameline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T19:47:27-08:00","id":1295188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aoi Cobalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1295016#post1295016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suggest that because the creators of the original Exalted suggested it, that demons lacked the capacity for growth. Which is why they were demons. Which is why demons were never a playable concept, unlike every other power group. Which is why Infernals existed, because demons were not a playable group.<br /> It's the demon's flaw, and why they are only tools. It's why the Primordials can't escape their prison, because they can't change what they are to become something different.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this the writer quote you're thinking of: <a href=\"http://nobilis.me/quote:on-demonic-morality\" target=\"_blank\">http://nobilis.me/quote<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />n-demonic-morality</a> ?<br /> <br /> Because I take away something very different from that than 'their defining intimacy is fixed', but I'll agree that it does seem to preclude a blood ape florist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3174-carl-ollivier","name":"Carl.ollivier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T01:15:47-08:00","id":1295261,"title":"","content":"I take it as if you get a demon of the 1st Circle to grow/change too much from the standard it\u2019s a mutant. 2nd ed had that take of a Neomah florist and how normal Neomah who worked in flesh and blood would view the one that worked in stem and petals as an abomination that needed genociding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T03:00:15-08:00","id":1295267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1295261#post1295261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>2nd ed had</b> that take of a Neomah florist and how normal Neomah who worked in flesh and blood would view the one that worked in stem and petals <b>as an abomination that needed genociding.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Ugh, of course it did. <br /> <br /> Wasn't it <i>the point</i> with Erembour, that denizens of the Demon City could be subject to drastic change or remaking? I don't see those twisted by her music getting rounded up and purged.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T03:33:37-08:00","id":1295274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1295261#post1295261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I take it as if you get a demon of the 1st Circle to grow/change too much from the standard it\u2019s a mutant. 2nd ed had that take of a Neomah florist and how normal Neomah who worked in flesh and blood would view the one that worked in stem and petals as an abomination that needed genociding.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so. <br /> <br /> In fact, that sounds pretty useful. Think of all the uses a Neomah that can cross in between different plants. Why, it may allow her to create GMOs! Think about it. Genetically engineering plants. <br /> <br /> Huh. Just got a new demon idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T04:04:31-08:00","id":1295278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1295160#post1295160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have my doubts about that though, at least by the time the first ed corebook was published I highly doubt they never would have thought the Lunars were going to be given any sort of character creation rules, unless they thought Exalted was a one book Gameline.</div> </div> </div> </div>By the time the first edition core was published Lunars were something else, but originally they were envisioned as monsters in league with the Fair Folk.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aoi Cobalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1295040#post1295040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You want demons to become other things, go ahead, it's your game. I find it's more interesting that demons are demons because they lack the capacity to change, tragically they will always be tools and never the protagonist.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm just vague on what the restrictions are or if it's actually meaningful in the context of the demons which have canonically changed. Like Gervesin changed pretty significantly because he killed one mortal and in that moment fell in love or Stanewald climbing the Imperial Mountain.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T06:15:03-08:00","id":1295294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Carl.ollivier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1295188#post1295188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is this the writer quote you're thinking of: <a href=\"http://nobilis.me/quote:on-demonic-morality\" target=\"_blank\">http://nobilis.me/quote<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />n-demonic-morality</a> ?<br /> <br /> Because I take away something very different from that than 'their defining intimacy is fixed', but I'll agree that it does seem to preclude a blood ape florist.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That, plus other writings and comments, and a whole slew of things.<br /> Maybe I'm wrong about defining intimacies, but as you see where I'm coming from, I'll take being partly wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24266-aoi-cobalt","name":"Aoi Cobalt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T06:25:21-08:00","id":1295297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hug Ninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1295278#post1295278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just vague on what the restrictions are or if it's actually meaningful in the context of the demons which have canonically changed. Like Gervesin changed pretty significantly because he killed one mortal and in that moment fell in love or Stanewald climbing the Imperial Mountain.</div> </div> </div> </div>In a metaphysical sense, until they did those things, they might have always carried the change in themselves. Gervesin would always be doomed to change when he killed a mortal, and now that he's done it, he can't go back to what he was before.<br /> A person would also change after killing their first mortal, but after time and further actions could change themselves into something else. Gervesin changed, but can't change again by himself. He is what he is now.<br /> <br /> Oops, I recalled Gervesin incorrectly. My error.<br /> Still, I would say he did not change himself, but was changed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24266,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24266-aoi-cobalt","user":"Aoi Cobalt","date":". 03-09-2019, 06:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24266-aoi-cobalt","name":"Aoi Cobalt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T06:37:04-08:00","id":1295299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1295261#post1295261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I take it as if you get a demon of the 1st Circle to grow/change too much from the standard it\u2019s a mutant. 2nd ed had that take of a Neomah florist and how normal Neomah who worked in flesh and blood would view the one that worked in stem and petals as an abomination that needed genociding.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1295267#post1295267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Wasn't it </span></span></span><i>the point</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> with Erembour, that denizens of the Demon City could be subject to drastic change or remaking? I don't see those twisted by her music getting rounded up and purged.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I would like to point out that I do support demons <i>being</i> changed, and making them into something that they were not.<br /> I just think that they can't change themselves.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24266-aoi-cobalt","name":"Aoi Cobalt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T06:44:25-08:00","id":1295302,"title":"","content":"Demons very definitely <i>can</i> change, going by 2e. It's the whole point of 1st circle demons becoming Citizens after all, distinguishing themselves from the others of their kind and moving beyond the typical purpose of their species.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Let us take men and give them the favor of the gods and use them as our champions against the Primordials, that we might overthrow them and play for ourselves the Games of Divinity.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2272-senresk","name":"senresk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T12:27:33-08:00","id":1295370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1295267#post1295267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ugh, of course it did. <br /> <br /> Wasn't it <i>the point</i> with Erembour, that denizens of the Demon City could be subject to drastic change or remaking? I don't see those twisted by her music getting rounded up and purged.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but they didn\u2019t hang around with unshadowed demons, it\u2019s like they had their own shadow ghetto and other demons would likely be torn up by them as they closed rank.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T12:30:56-08:00","id":1295372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hug Ninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1295278#post1295278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the time the first edition core was published Lunars were something else, but originally they were envisioned as monsters in league with the Fair Folk.<br /> <br /> I'm just vague on what the restrictions are or if it's actually meaningful in the context of the demons which have canonically changed. Like Gervesin changed pretty significantly because he killed one mortal and in that moment fell in love or Stanewald climbing the Imperial Mountain.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but nobody cares about changes before the core, it wasn\u2019t a book yet and at best it was only notes. Nobody goes by something that was only in the head of the developers and was changed the moment they revealed it on paper.<br /> <br /> <br /> And I believe the poster is talking about 1st Circle demons, nobody questioned 2nd and 3rd circles changed and grew.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T15:07:03-08:00","id":1295398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>senresk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1295302#post1295302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demons very definitely <i>can</i> change, going by 2e. It's the whole point of 1st circle demons becoming Citizens after all, distinguishing themselves from the others of their kind and moving beyond the typical purpose of their species.</div> </div> </div> </div>But for all they do, they are still the same first circle demon they started as. They do not change. They may have another talent, or worked on polishing a useful skill, but they remain what they are with a perceived higher value. A 1st circle blood ape citizen may be the same quality as our Creation merc blood ape, but when all is said and done they are both blood apes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24266-aoi-cobalt","name":"Aoi Cobalt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T15:15:48-08:00","id":1295402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aoi Cobalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1295398#post1295398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But for all they do, they are still the same first circle demon they started as. They do not change. They may have another talent, or worked on polishing a useful skill, but they remain what they are with a perceived higher value. A 1st circle blood ape citizen may be the same quality as our Creation merc blood ape, but when all is said and done they are both blood apes.</div> </div> </div> </div>.... You can say the same about humans. <br /> <br /> Was this supposed to be insightful?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T15:35:43-08:00","id":1295408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1295372#post1295372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah but nobody cares about changes before the core, it wasn\u2019t a book yet and at best it was only notes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless people learn of the original version and prefer it or it explains a lot about the game we have.<br /> See- The 2.5 errata of Fair Folk that was based on an unused outline from 1e Fair Folk and people who want Dragon-Blooded in the core.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nobody goes by something that was only in the head of the developers and was changed the moment they revealed it on paper.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you think the community knows about this stuff?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I believe the poster is talking about 1st Circle demons, nobody questioned 2nd and 3rd circles changed and grew.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, he replied to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T16:48:50-08:00","id":1295413,"title":"","content":"On the floral Neomah thing the example seems to be getting used wrong here. First this was not a deliberate alteration of the demon by itself, this was a Wyld mutation. So this was hardly, &quot;Hey you heard Agra decided he wanted to learn the trumpet? Let's kill that freak.&quot; Second the entry says that most demons don't actually give a crap so long as the alteration doesn't impede their inherent nature, the example being that a blood ape with a frog tongue just uses a frog tongue when it wants to lap up blood and the like now.<br /> <br /> The only issue came up when a demon suffered a fundamental nature alteration. (Noting that derangments inflicted by the Wyld on demons are alterations of the demon's nature.) At which point the options for the demon were, mutation reversal, dying, or becoming something different than what it was. Now that last one seems to argue against the whole demons can't change thing, but one could also accept it as just meaning the demon would need to resign itself to suffering more mutations and derangments until such time as it is likely to be regarded by its former kin as something like them, but not originally of them at the minimum.<br /> <br /> What this also means is that a demon deciding to move into Creation would just be likely to adapt its situation to fit it doing its thing. So a bloodape would go into a field where it could crush things and drink blood and marrow without much difficulty, or at the least keep that as a big deal in its life. A Neomah might decide to become a courtesan or whatever just probably still charging its tissue sample prices to be able to still work on the whole fleshcrafting thing. They might choose some other field entirely from those, though I'd imagine the demon would follow its skillset, just those things would still be central as those are core to what the demon is. So a Perroneles ,the Living Armor, that's learned sales and how to do the merchant thing isn't getting executed by its kin unless the thing refuses to slither across people and become armor anymore. If its gained a fondness for taking apprentices in some field and making them wear it, so it can be close at hand to protect them and educate them; then such is just a weird quirk of that particular Perroneles.<br /> <br /> <br /> * Source; Compass of Celestial Directions 2: The Wyld pg 66","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T21:24:23-08:00","id":1295484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1295413#post1295413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the floral Neomah thing the example seems to be getting used wrong here. First this was not a deliberate alteration of the demon by itself, this was a Wyld mutation. So this was hardly, &amp;quot;Hey you heard Agra decided he wanted to learn the trumpet? Let's kill that freak.&amp;quot; Second the entry says that most demons don't actually give a crap so long as the alteration doesn't impede their inherent nature, the example being that a blood ape with a frog tongue just uses a frog tongue when it wants to lap up blood and the like now.<br /> <br /> The only issue came up when a demon suffered a fundamental nature alteration. (Noting that derangments inflicted by the Wyld on demons are alterations of the demon's nature.) At which point the options for the demon were, mutation reversal, dying, or becoming something different than what it was. Now that last one seems to argue against the whole demons can't change thing, but one could also accept it as just meaning the demon would need to resign itself to suffering more mutations and derangments until such time as it is likely to be regarded by its former kin as something like them, but not originally of them at the minimum.<br /> <br /> What this also means is that a demon deciding to move into Creation would just be likely to adapt its situation to fit it doing its thing. So a bloodape would go into a field where it could crush things and drink blood and marrow without much difficulty, or at the least keep that as a big deal in its life. A Neomah might decide to become a courtesan or whatever just probably still charging its tissue sample prices to be able to still work on the whole fleshcrafting thing. They might choose some other field entirely from those, though I'd imagine the demon would follow its skillset, just those things would still be central as those are core to what the demon is. So a Perroneles ,the Living Armor, that's learned sales and how to do the merchant thing isn't getting executed by its kin unless the thing refuses to slither across people and become armor anymore. If its gained a fondness for taking apprentices in some field and making them wear it, so it can be close at hand to protect them and educate them; then such is just a weird quirk of that particular Perroneles.<br /> <br /> <br /> * Source; Compass of Celestial Directions 2: The Wyld pg 66</div> </div> </div> </div>How is it being used wrong? I mentioned a fundamental change, I didn\u2019t feel like mentioning something like a blood ape growing wings or an extra arm because He\u2019ll already has mutation pits that do that and other blood apes don\u2019t care. I mentioned the Neomah part because it was pertinent to the discussion, one crafts plants instead of flesh is a freak among their Kin. I don\u2019t think Demons are immune to physical Wyld mutations, that is ridiculous, the point is the Wyld isn\u2019t limited to simply giving you an Extra Eye it can change you much more profoundly, and I didn\u2019t mention the Wyld because it didn\u2019t seem pertinent. And besides Neomah are often isolated from others of their own kind anways so I doubt a Floral Neomah is in much danger from other Neomah unless collected into a demon seraglio, and other demons don\u2019t care, they aren\u2019t your kinsmen.<br /> <br /> And I\u2019m pretty sure A Blood Ape lost in Creation could say fit in and find a mate with something like a Buck Ogre. There is a certain amount of leeway.<br /> <br /> I do believe though if you say summoned a Blood Ape and ordered him to stay in a Library and read all the books that itself could spark a fundamental change. Because I believe it would likely break and become unhinged from forcing such an unaccustomed lifestyle in it, but I believe if you did it to enough Eurymanthoi every now and then you would get one that start to change.<br /> <br /> By the books Demons of the First Circle seem to be between God and Elemental. They aren\u2019t as immortal as gods, but cults can move them in that direction, and before Gods couldn\u2019t teach themselves charms outside of Martial Arts, or Sorcery. Elementals could and it would cause them to evolve over time, and Demons could as well but we don\u2019t know what happens to them, I had a couple threads about it over the last decade and I\u2019m open to a lot of options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T21:28:07-08:00","id":1295486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hug Ninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1295408#post1295408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless people learn of the original version and prefer it or it explains a lot about the game we have.<br /> See- The 2.5 errata of Fair Folk that was based on an unused outline from 1e Fair Folk and people who want Dragon-Blooded in the core.<br /> <br /> <br /> How do you think the community knows about this stuff?<br /> <br /> <br /> No, he replied to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes but it\u2019s still the 2.5 Fairfolk, it\u2019s a fully realized concept, it\u2019s not the Half Birthed Early Draft of Fairfolk. Besides a lot of the change is mostly making them blend well with nonfairfolk games, because By the time Fairfolk got their first book they gave them too many Fairfolk exclusive rules that made them a headache. People like 2.5 Raksha because they are fun and relatively easy to insert in a game, not because they vaguely resemble a hypothetical Fairfolk 0.75.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T22:13:56-08:00","id":1295496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1295484#post1295484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How is it being used wrong? I mentioned a fundamental change, I didn\u2019t feel like mentioning something like a blood ape growing wings or an extra arm because He\u2019ll already has mutation pits that do that and other blood apes don\u2019t care. I mentioned the Neomah part because it was pertinent to the discussion, one crafts plants instead of flesh is a freak among their Kin. I don\u2019t think Demons are immune to physical Wyld mutations, that is ridiculous, the point is the Wyld isn\u2019t limited to simply giving you an Extra Eye it can change you much more profoundly, and I didn\u2019t mention the Wyld because it didn\u2019t seem pertinent. And besides Neomah are often isolated from others of their own kind anways so I doubt a Floral Neomah is in much danger from other Neomah unless collected into a demon seraglio, and other demons don\u2019t care, they aren\u2019t your kinsmen.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well first because the example Neomah wasn't actually listed as gaining or using its ability to bind flesh to plants, or gaining an interest in using its abilities to craft plants. The exact reference was a Neomah that has become obsessed with collecting roses and no longer does the fleshworking of their kind would be considered an abomination. So on the first part your actually cited example is wrong. Though excusable as the picture on the next page has what is ,presumably, a hypothetical neomah mixing a rat (guessing on tail length there) and a rose. <br /> <br /> Honestly, creating hybrid offspring from plants and animals seems like it would be up the Neomah preference alley considering they're also known for enabling offspring between spirits and mortals. Probably riskier if its abilities are entirely bound within fauna now, but then that is why it brings up the option of ceasing to be their old species as an alternative to death, or reversing the process. Particularly since, as preciously noted, a demon capable of doing the neomah thing with different plants would probably be really useful and the demon in question might enjoy the challenges and prospects of the ability set.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1295484#post1295484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I\u2019m pretty sure A Blood Ape lost in Creation could say fit in and find a mate with something like a Buck Ogre. There is a certain amount of leeway.<br /> <br /> I do believe though if you say summoned a Blood Ape and ordered him to stay in a Library and read all the books that itself could spark a fundamental change. Because I believe it would likely break and become unhinged from forcing such an unaccustomed lifestyle in it, but I believe if you did it to enough Eurymanthoi every now and then you would get one that start to change.<br /> <br /> By the books Demons of the First Circle seem to be between God and Elemental. They aren\u2019t as immortal as gods, but cults can move them in that direction, and before Gods couldn\u2019t teach themselves charms outside of Martial Arts, or Sorcery. Elementals could and it would cause them to evolve over time, and Demons could as well but we don\u2019t know what happens to them, I had a couple threads about it over the last decade and I\u2019m open to a lot of options.</div> </div> </div> </div>And you've missed the entire point of the clarification I gave. The entry cited was that demons are given a fair amount of leeway on how much an alteration happens before it potentially brings down lethal ramifications. Basically so long as they don't end up altered in a way that goes against the point of their own species demons tend to not care (conflicts between individuals aside.) A Blood Ape forced to study an entire library might sufferer mental alterations, but it isn't like the other apes are gonna kill it on the spot because it learned some stuff.* Nothing about demons being immune to physical Wyld mutations, particularly since I specifically brought up the frog tongue thing from the book, or that the Wyld was the only way to do it. I brought it up because it was being discussed as if any alteration to a demon meant that it was purged when that wasn't even implied in the book.<br /> <br /> <br /> *May still end up dead rather quickly though. I mean the point of the Blood Apes is crushing, killing, drinking blood, and sucking the marrow from bones, so they tend to be kind of fond of the activity. Depending on how long it took to read all the books and whether or not it ever had an opportunity to do some of the killing it may have a serious need to kill something when its all done which could go poorly depending on how and where it releases said urge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T22:19:51-08:00","id":1295497,"title":"","content":"An amusing one since it briefly came up earlier. Did have a demon bartender once in campaign since the Malfeas book in 2nd had an entry on bars in Malfeas. Secret menu stuff was the various drinks served from Malfeas, which included sensations and feelings as drinks. I uhm may have had a drink that solely existed for instant sobriety and torture that was literally a hangover after an all night bender in a bottle. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> None of the party wanted to try the one that let you feel a peaceful death in your sleep surrounded by loved ones though. Barkeep thought it was sensible, though the book did mention it was more dangerous for demons than mortals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T22:26:44-08:00","id":1295498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1295496#post1295496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well first because the example Neomah wasn't actually listed as gaining or using its ability to bind flesh to plants, or gaining an interest in using its abilities to craft plants. The exact reference was a Neomah that has become obsessed with collecting roses and no longer does the fleshworking of their kind would be considered an abomination. So on the first part your actually cited example is wrong. Though excusable as the picture on the next page has what is ,presumably, a hypothetical neomah mixing a rat (guessing on tail length there) and a rose. <br /> <br /> Honestly, creating hybrid offspring from plants and animals seems like it would be up the Neomah preference alley considering they're also known for enabling offspring between spirits and mortals. Probably riskier if its abilities are entirely bound within fauna now, but then that is why it brings up the option of ceasing to be their old species as an alternative to death, or reversing the process. Particularly since, as preciously noted, a demon capable of doing the neomah thing with different plants would probably be really useful and the demon in question might enjoy the challenges and prospects of the ability set.<br /> <br /> <br /> And you've missed the entire point of the clarification I gave. The entry cited was that demons are given a fair amount of leeway on how much an alteration happens before it potentially brings down lethal ramifications. Basically so long as they don't end up altered in a way that goes against the point of their own species demons tend to not care (conflicts between individuals aside.) A Blood Ape forced to study an entire library might sufferer mental alterations, but it isn't like the other apes are gonna kill it on the spot because it learned some stuff.* Nothing about demons being immune to physical Wyld mutations, particularly since I specifically brought up the frog tongue thing from the book, or that the Wyld was the only way to do it. I brought it up because it was being discussed as if any alteration to a demon meant that it was purged when that wasn't even implied in the book.<br /> <br /> <br /> *May still end up dead rather quickly though. I mean the point of the Blood Apes is crushing, killing, drinking blood, and sucking the marrow from bones, so they tend to be kind of fond of the activity. Depending on how long it took to read all the books and whether or not it ever had an opportunity to do some of the killing it may have a serious need to kill something when its all done which could go poorly depending on how and where it releases said urge.</div> </div> </div> </div>I may be wrong on the plant point, though as you pointed out the picture implied a plant affinity.<br /> <br /> And I\u2019m not missing the point with my blood ape Examples, I was agreeing with you, so please chill the hostility. (Seriously what is up with this forum it waxes and wanes in hostility and aggression every year, or maybe it\u2019s just certain individuals).<br /> <br /> And I never said a Blood Ape that learns to read would get beaten to death for it, they would probably be likely to be in charge of gangs due to being more skilled, unless it snuffed out their Bloodlust.<br /> <br /> And do you think a Blood Ape will finish all books in a library (purposely ambiguous size but even tiny libraries should have more then enough books for most people) before they limit break (or in third ed with not mention of them having a limit track just flat out normal mentally breaking).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T23:55:25-08:00","id":1295511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1295498#post1295498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may be wrong on the plant point, though as you pointed out the picture implied a plant affinity.<br /> <br /> And I\u2019m not missing the point with my blood ape Examples, I was agreeing with you, so please chill the hostility. (Seriously what is up with this forum it waxes and wanes in hostility and aggression every year, or maybe it\u2019s just certain individuals).<br /> <br /> And I never said a Blood Ape that learns to read would get beaten to death for it, they would probably be likely to be in charge of gangs due to being more skilled, unless it snuffed out their Bloodlust.<br /> <br /> And do you think a Blood Ape will finish all books in a library (purposely ambiguous size but even tiny libraries should have more then enough books for most people) before they limit break (or in third ed with not mention of them having a limit track just flat out normal mentally breaking).</div> </div> </div> </div>Partially a tone thing. When you start out a response as, &quot;In what way am I wrong?&quot; You come off as defensive, add in that you have this tendency for your writing style to come off as belittling to flat out insulting your entire thing comes off as a prolonged &quot;I'm right, you're wrong and an idiot for disagreeing with me.&quot; Your blood ape scenario , for example, did not come off as being a hypothetical for other means through which a demon might be altered, but an attempt to demean and rebuke the other party.<br /> <br /> As for the Blood Ape, I hate their real I can never spell it right, reading all the books in a library I don't think it has a choice in the matter. I mean you said summoned and bound, so while I'd have to check the old rules to be certain taskbound overruled the year and a day portion of a binding. There's a good chance it'll lose it a few times and the library will likely finish this thing's binding with fewer books than it started, but the blood ape will read all of them if nothing prevents it from doing so. It was why we used to have those arguments on people saying that if the Realm were smart they'd stake a wheel in the middle of a desert or something and bind each 2nd and 3rd circle demon they could summon to turn the wheel. Arguing that such would bind them forever as things like That Which Calls to Darkness and The Living Tower are just turning a wheel around a pillar for the next millenia or so.*<br /> <br /> <br /> *I managed to get the Zenith in my, possibly shortlived, 3E Solar campaign to have formerly been the mayor of a town founded by a 2nd circle demon to ensure the continuing turning of a wheel from that scenario.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T01:00:24-08:00","id":1295523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1295511#post1295511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Partially a tone thing. When you start out a response as, &amp;quot;In what way am I wrong?&amp;quot; You come off as defensive, add in that you have this tendency for your writing style to come off as belittling to flat out insulting your entire thing comes off as a prolonged &amp;quot;I'm right, you're wrong and an idiot for disagreeing with me.&amp;quot; Your blood ape scenario , for example, did not come off as being a hypothetical for other means through which a demon might be altered, but an attempt to demean and rebuke the other party.<br /> <br /> As for the Blood Ape, I hate their real I can never spell it right, reading all the books in a library I don't think it has a choice in the matter. I mean you said summoned and bound, so while I'd have to check the old rules to be certain taskbound overruled the year and a day portion of a binding. There's a good chance it'll lose it a few times and the library will likely finish this thing's binding with fewer books than it started, but the blood ape will read all of them if nothing prevents it from doing so. It was why we used to have those arguments on people saying that if the Realm were smart they'd stake a wheel in the middle of a desert or something and bind each 2nd and 3rd circle demon they could summon to turn the wheel. Arguing that such would bind them forever as things like That Which Calls to Darkness and The Living Tower are just turning a wheel around a pillar for the next millenia or so.*<br /> <br /> <br /> *I managed to get the Zenith in my, possibly shortlived, 3E Solar campaign to have formerly been the mayor of a town founded by a 2nd circle demon to ensure the continuing turning of a wheel from that scenario.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was defensive. But as you literally just quoted I will point out if I believe I am incorrect or remembered something poorly. I\u2019ve been on the whitewolf/onyx path forums for like 15. Years I think, I seldom got into arguements. Yet here in this current Exalted Forum I see people arguing all the time, in my opinion petty petty ass stuff. Outside of the Scion Forums from ten years back (probably worst garbage fire I can recall on my time on the Internet, anyone remember when they invaded the old Exalted Forums when I referred to their actions as Childish and they tried tearing down other posters and even authors as collateral damage? We haven\u2019t gotten that bad here yet) the current Exalted Forum from my opinion has been the most agressive/hostile/elitist of the forums. I answer in kind, well almost I like to think I\u2019m not overtly insulting just curt and not interested the dance of Forum politics where I see people try to see how close they can get to insulting each other without getting called out by a mod for stepping the line. I see people out right call each other\u2019s opinions worthless, oh so carefully imply some not very nice things about others.<br /> <br /> So yeah call me a cosmic mirror because people are receiving what they are putting out. Like this thread, last two people I talked here you nalak and hugs. I know I\u2019ve interacted with you two before, I don\u2019t remember about what but all I can recall is aggression, which I forgot until I get posts by both of you with very distinct tones and I remember oh hey this is familiar. And if I don\u2019t post for months I\u2019ll return and flat out forget Even countalucard, but I quickly remember him because of his very \u201cparticular\u201d posting style.<br /> <br /> People are allowed to disagree here, people are even allowed to *gasp* be wrong about something concerning the Gameline. People are even allowed to address others unwarmly as long as you are not flat out insulting. But don\u2019t stamp your foot when your \u201clessers\u201d are too I unenlightened to not agree with you. Some of us might be dense. It\u2019s not a crime to not agree with every point of a discussion, and dogpiling won\u2019t change that. Sometimes there is some dissonance in communication. You might not be arguing what you think you are. It\u2019s not a crime to disagree, even if you are out numbered. Probably shouldn\u2019t be obviously aggressively frustrated when someone disagrees with you though.<br /> <br /> Like I\u2019ve been on the Exalted forums in ages long past, people used to be a \u201clot\u201d more chill. Then again we have had about this level of \u201cughh\u201d before, if I recall though that passed when we started getting more content. Yet here and right now I don\u2019t see it passing. We may get more people, I\u2019m not sure, but a good amount of the Forum is still agressive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T01:14:10-08:00","id":1295524,"title":"","content":"Also the reason why the Realm (do you mean the Old Realm because the current Realm can\u2019t easily bind 2nd and 3rd Circle Demons) didn\u2019t bind all the 2nd and 3rd Circle Demons is for a few Reasons I wager. One they are very particularly useful Slaves, useful beyond measure for certain tasks. Two bonds can sometimes be broken or demons banished, if done to one demon it can be done to the Entire Infernal Host, and they would now have a very solid reason to hate your Civilization, even more then before when the Totality of their beings were Castrated, humiliated, ritually mutilated, and enslaved. Now each and every component has a specific reason to hate you, like say an intimacy of Major or Defining level. Remember demons don\u2019t hate you when they are bound but after they are free to access how they were treated and make up their own mind.<br /> <br /> And Third, and perhaps most damning of all doing so would give the Yozis the feeling like they have virtually nothing to loose, and as mentioned in that past edition the Universe didn\u2019t want that because they would be free to unlock the various Seals and Curses and Omnipotent hatred they have stored around and that would make Creation a very unpleasant place, if it even survives for long. And since Yozis can actually wear their component and descendant souls like a hand in a puppet (while also breaking their bindings incidental) they would be in a prime position to smite the Universe in one gathered Mass. But that last part is kind of a secret, but back in the day they knew they would still be able to do something unpleasant if given a reason too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T04:26:24-07:00","id":1295532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1295402#post1295402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> .... You can say the same about humans.<br /> <br /> Was this supposed to be insightful?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you can't. A human can become what it want to be (within limits, of course). Mercenary, florist, monk, blacksmith. There are forces against this, of course (tradition, family honor, parental wishes, etc), but those are just influences that can be cast off.<br /> A blood ape is only ever a murder machine, because that is what it was made to do. It can get a personality, learn things to make it better than the rest, but when all is said and done, it is just a murder machine. A blood ape can't stop being a murder machine and be a florist unless someone or something MAKES it be a florist. It can't wake up one morning and decide that its tired of being a murder machine and now it wants to be a florist. <br /> People can decide to change themselves. Not often, but the capability is there. It isn't there for demons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24266-aoi-cobalt","name":"Aoi Cobalt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T04:47:12-07:00","id":1295535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aoi Cobalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1295532#post1295532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, you can't. A human can become what it want to be (within limits, of course). Mercenary, florist, monk, blacksmith. There are forces against this, of course (tradition, family honor, parental wishes, etc), but those are just influences that can be cast off.<br /> A blood ape is only ever a murder machine, because that is what it was made to do. It can get a personality, learn things to make it better than the rest, but when all is said and done, it is just a murder machine. A blood ape can't stop being a murder machine and be a florist unless someone or something MAKES it be a florist. It can't wake up one morning and decide that its tired of being a murder machine and now it wants to be a florist.<br /> People can decide to change themselves. Not often, but the capability is there. It isn't there for demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um.. a blood ape can become a florist. <br /> <br /> A very murdery florist. But yes. As stated before, you can say the same thing about a human. I mean, unless you say that anyone can become a mercenary or blacksmith. Besides, weren't humans made as prayer batteries? <br /> <br /> Look. This: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A blood ape can't stop being a murder machine and be a florist unless someone or something MAKES it be a florist. It can't wake up one morning and decide that its tired of being a murder machine and now it wants to be a florist. </div> </div> </div>Applies to all humans too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T05:20:32-07:00","id":1295539,"title":"","content":"Fun factoid: You can be a murderer and a florist simultaneously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T05:33:20-07:00","id":1295542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1295539#post1295539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fun factoid: You can be a murderer and a florist simultaneously.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. Now that's a good serial killer backstory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T05:50:22-07:00","id":1295544,"title":"","content":"I am not sure that any particular species of serf is more or less bound by their nature against their aspirations, than is true for humanity. But I am also not sure if their aspirations tend as much towards diverse forms, absent external pressure. That is, tentatively, they are no less free willed than humans, but they do not have the same variety in where their will is pushing them.<br /> <br /> On the evil of demons I would say my impression is; they tend to combine beauty and grotesquerie, they tend to have strong creative urges and purpose we would find at least somewhat admirable, they tend not to be driven by an overriding moral conviction or malevolence of any sort (exceptions - &quot;The Lions Sent Into The World&quot;, etc.). They in general the form and nature they are given obeys the statement that &quot;Few things in the Demon City do not ultimately serve (the end of vengeance against the world). Its horrors exist to torment and kill. Its beauties exist to break the mortal heart&quot;, but this is a statement of their making by the Yozis, not their psychology and intent. (And of course this clashes with the 2e emergent meme thing that pretty much all the demons are the same as in the Primordial Age, but that's not my personal headcanon, rather than that all the demons were changed fundamentally. YMMV.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T06:28:40-07:00","id":1295547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1295523#post1295523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So yeah call me a cosmic mirror because people are receiving what they are putting out. Like this thread, last two people I talked here you nalak and hugs. I know I\u2019ve interacted with you two before, I don\u2019t remember about what but all I can recall is aggression, which I forgot until I get posts by both of you with very distinct tones and I remember oh hey this is familiar. And if I don\u2019t post for months I\u2019ll return and flat out forget Even countalucard, but I quickly remember him because of his very \u201cparticular\u201d posting style.<br /> <br /> People are allowed to disagree here, people are even allowed to *gasp* be wrong about something concerning the Gameline. People are even allowed to address others unwarmly as long as you are not flat out insulting. But don\u2019t stamp your foot when your \u201clessers\u201d are too I unenlightened to not agree with you. Some of us might be dense. It\u2019s not a crime to not agree with every point of a discussion, and dogpiling won\u2019t change that. Sometimes there is some dissonance in communication. You might not be arguing what you think you are. It\u2019s not a crime to disagree, even if you are out numbered. Probably shouldn\u2019t be obviously aggressively frustrated when someone disagrees with you though.<br /> <br /> Like I\u2019ve been on the Exalted forums in ages long past, people used to be a \u201clot\u201d more chill. Then again we have had about this level of \u201cughh\u201d before, if I recall though that passed when we started getting more content. Yet here and right now I don\u2019t see it passing. We may get more people, I\u2019m not sure, but a good amount of the Forum is still agressive.</div> </div> </div> </div><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">That's not being a cosmic mirror, that's having an axe to grind. Responding to perceived hostility in kind isn't an ideal strategy at the best of times but when it occured in a different discussion and possibly several months ago? That makes the forums considerably less 'chill' than people disagreeing.<br /> <br /> You're also going on an off-topic rant about the conduct of multiple users and the perceived state of the forum in a thread about how demons behave. You should maybe not do that? </span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T06:41:09-07:00","id":1295553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1295547#post1295547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">That's not being a cosmic mirror, that's having an axe to grind. Responding to perceived hostility in kind isn't an ideal strategy at the best of times but when it occured in a different discussion and possibly several months ago? That makes the forums considerably less 'chill' than people disagreeing.<br /> <br /> You're also going on an off-topic rant about the conduct of multiple users and the perceived state of the forum in a thread about how demons behave. You should maybe not do that? </span></b></div> </div> </div> </div>I said I only respond discourteouslyafter someone has responded that way to me in the same thread. As I said I don\u2019t even remember them until they act in a a familiar fashion. Besides this thread you are quoting where I explain myself (and I don\u2019t think even there), point to me where have I broken any rules. All I\u2019ve done is called out people. I\u2019ll back off but I am asking politely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T10:47:45-07:00","id":1295585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1295535#post1295535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Applies to all humans too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. You can make a human change. You can make a demon change.<br /> <br /> But the problem that you seem to be ducking is that a human can change themselves, without an outside force.<br /> A demon can not. Without an outside force, a demon remains what it is. Which is what the Yozi's want out of demons.<br /> <br /> This is the biggest difference between humans and demons. <br /> <br /> Yes, I know the Yozi's made humans too. And after seeing what that lead to, they decided that there would be no more of that, thank you very much.<br /> <br /> Or are you claiming that humans can not make their own changes, that free will does not exist, and humans are just prayer batteries (because you know they still are).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24266-aoi-cobalt","name":"Aoi Cobalt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T10:49:45-07:00","id":1295586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1295539#post1295539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fun factoid: You can be a murderer and a florist simultaneously.</div> </div> </div> </div>A human, yes.<br /> A 1st circle demon...? Only if there was a need for murderous florists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24266-aoi-cobalt","name":"Aoi Cobalt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T14:38:21-07:00","id":1295653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aoi Cobalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1295585#post1295585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the problem that you seem to be ducking is that a human can change themselves, without an outside force.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is <i>definitely</i> true? That's news to me - did someone manage to resolve the whole &quot;free will vs. determinism&quot; <i>thing</i> while I was having my Exalted session?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 03-10-2019, 05:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T15:18:51-07:00","id":1295666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1295653#post1295653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is <i>definitely</i> true? That's news to me - did someone manage to resolve the whole &quot;free will vs. determinism&quot; <i>thing</i> while I was having my Exalted session?</div> </div> </div> </div>So you are down for option 2, that free will does not exist for humans in the game. Well that certainly answers a lot of questions. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24266-aoi-cobalt","name":"Aoi Cobalt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T15:21:54-07:00","id":1295667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aoi Cobalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1295666#post1295666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you are down for option 2, that free will does not exist for humans in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just don't feel that humans in the game should <b>concretely </b>be said to have libertarian free will when we in real life cannot. If the actions of humans in the Exalted setting are somehow mystically <b>not</b> the products of tens to millions of large and tiny, visible and invisible factors that weigh on the decisions they make... well, that basically makes them weird aliens, to me.<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 03-10-2019, 06:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T19:58:17-07:00","id":1295724,"title":"","content":"I think putting down that Demons cannot change themselves, especially when we have several canon examples of them doing so, makes the game poorer and cuts off story ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T04:25:07-07:00","id":1295755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1295724#post1295724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think putting down that Demons cannot change themselves, especially when we have several canon examples of them doing so, makes the game poorer and cuts off story ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once again, I feel there is a meaningful difference between something changing a demon and a demon changing itself. (Free will vs organic programming debate aside).<br /> We already have had the writers tell us that demons can not be heroic. They lack that ability.<br /> This means they also lack the heroic ability to decide that they want to redeem themselves (unlike humans, who can, as per the Abyssal redemption trope).<br /> The easiest way I can see demons not having any ability to choose these is that they also lack the ability to choose to be something they are not. For example, we know there are demonic bartenders exist. I would say that existing demons are not turned into bartenders, but a 1st circle species of demonic bartender exists (summonable for your next exotic Cynis party!). If the need for a demonic florist exists, then a 1st circle demon florist exists.<br /> <br /> Yes, this cuts off several story ideas. But then the writers decided that those story ideas weren't part of Exalted (just like several story ideas are cut off because Creation has a celestial bureaucracy of many gods and no reward for good souls and punishment for wicked souls). If the current writers of 3rd Edition wish to change this, they will inform us (in due time, no doubt).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24266-aoi-cobalt","name":"Aoi Cobalt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T04:36:04-07:00","id":1295758,"title":"","content":"Wait. Redeem?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T05:42:44-07:00","id":1295771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1295758#post1295758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait. Redeem?</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that not a heroic story?<br /> I have chosen to be an avatar of death, and to kill the whole world.<br /> Wait, I think that I have mischosen. Instead of just continuing easily down this path, I will heroicly fight my fate and redeem myself.<br /> Standard Abyssal storyline. <br /> <br /> Demons lack heroic options, so you can not have one decide that it will no longer be what it is, and become something that is not a &quot;Creature of Darkness&quot;. Therefore not redemption stories for demons can exist.<br /> <br /> And if a demon can not make a choice to change itself in that way, it stands to reason that it also lacks the ability to change itself in other ways, that is to deny its demonic purpose. A blood ape was made for a purpose. It can not change the its purpose is, it can not become something is was not meant to be. It can be more competent and better at what it does, but it is still a blood ape.<br /> <br /> As a Solar, I can make it change. With my mighty powers, I can make it a blood ape florist. <br /> But the blood ape on its own can not choose to become a florist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24266-aoi-cobalt","name":"Aoi Cobalt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T06:21:09-07:00","id":1295783,"title":"","content":"..... Did you not...<br /> <br /> Have you read Exalted? Like, enough to pick up on the themes and subtext?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T06:41:50-07:00","id":1295793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1295783#post1295783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">..... Did you not...<br /> <br /> Have you read Exalted? Like, enough to pick up on the themes and subtext?</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>This is rude. Please rethink your approach. </b></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T06:47:37-07:00","id":1295797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1295793#post1295793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>This is rude. Please rethink your approach. </b></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Alright fine. I'll humour you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T06:52:59-07:00","id":1295799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aoi Cobalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1295771#post1295771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that not a heroic story?<br /> I have chosen to be an avatar of death, and to kill the whole world.<br /> Wait, I think that I have mischosen. Instead of just continuing easily down this path, I will heroicly fight my fate and redeem myself.<br /> Standard Abyssal storyline. <br /> <br /> Demons lack heroic options, so you can not have one decide that it will no longer be what it is, and become something that is not a &amp;quot;Creature of Darkness&amp;quot;. Therefore not redemption stories for demons can exist.<br /> <br /> And if a demon can not make a choice to change itself in that way, it stands to reason that it also lacks the ability to change itself in other ways, that is to deny its demonic purpose. A blood ape was made for a purpose. It can not change the its purpose is, it can not become something is was not meant to be. It can be more competent and better at what it does, but it is still a blood ape.<br /> <br /> As a Solar, I can make it change. With my mighty powers, I can make it a blood ape florist. <br /> But the blood ape on its own can not choose to become a florist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exalted says much about morality, by saying nothing at all.<br /> <br /> Creature of darkness? That's not a crime. That just means youre on the sun's shitlist. Sesseljae eat poison. Eat disease. And cure wounds. And are very compassionate. They're creatures of darkness. So are neomah, who are more compassion and trustworthy than the average mortal. And so are Angelkyae, harpists who only desire to play music.<br /> <br /> Creature of darkness? That means notbing. When they say 'demon', they mean its alien and odd. Not strange.<br /> <br /> Also, there was an entire school written up in malfeas compass. An agatae that learnt thaumaturgy and sorcery. He got it from a sorcerer, then decided to start up a school. No commands. No force. From philosophical jewel wasp that spends its days contemplating alien philosophies to teacher.<br /> <br /> And hell, he has students. Students wishing to better themselves and learn thaumaturgy and sorcery. How is that not becoming greater and something different than before?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T08:07:09-07:00","id":1295821,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jenna Moran</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a way, a good description for what they've lost is the capacity for heroism. It's that thing that stands between Solars and most WoD splats, that thing that lets you be grander than life without being monstrous. Solars can still forge a utopia, although canonically they won't. Demons don't have that option.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jenna Moran</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">They can still be Raksi. (And worse.) They can still be <i>better</i> than Raksi. But they can't be the thing that the people who complain about Raksi would rather Lunars be. There's no healing for them as the world of Exalted stands. And that's why you have the demons that are all about pain and deceit and stuff\u2014-not because it's what they are, but because it's the only direction they can go. They've lost their protagonist slot, more severely even than the Abyssals, and the only way to get it back is to be PCs in a really deviant game.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><br /> <br /> Yes, Exalted is a huge heroic game. Yes, that means heroic redemption is up for grabs as part of the setting.<br /> But also as part of the setting, demons are denyed it. Sad, but true. Everyone except demons can get redemption.<br /> <br /> Creature of Darkness is only a tag, as you said. Everyone can try and get that tag removed.., except for demons. <br /> <br /> That is why I see demons as limited. Because they got deliberately limited in the setting.<br /> And, until they broke the setting rules for Infernals, Yozi and demons were the only power group that could never have their plans come to pass.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24266-aoi-cobalt","name":"Aoi Cobalt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T08:58:05-07:00","id":1296151,"title":"","content":"Well, that certainly killed the subject.<br /> <br /> But while I'm on it, I'm none too happy about what the 2nd Edition writers did to the city of Malfeas. They took what should have been one of the most alien things in Exalted and turned it into the city of Nexus for demons. I understand why, because with Infernals around, you had to have a playable city of Malfeas. But somehow it just didn't keep the alien feel. It felt like a human city with demons instead of humans.<br /> I fervently hope that when the 3rd Edition writers get around to the city of Malfeas, they make it an alien and strange place (except for the area around where they keep the GSP, that I would expect to be a false front of what demons mistakenly think a human city is like, but off by enough to be disquieting).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24266-aoi-cobalt","name":"Aoi Cobalt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T05:55:07-07:00","id":1305451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1294786#post1294786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which human culture; there are lots of them.<br /> <br /> Even a blood ape might fit in with something like, say, a mercenary army. Not every blood ape, but the kind that has a higher sense of camaraderie and sees better opportunities for violence and feeding by serving a specialised function within a fighting group.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, in fact it might be said to be one of the linchpins of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/116419-giving-the-little-guy-some-room-to-shine-first-circle-demons-as-individuals\">a NPC</a> that would become something of a reference in my use of 1st circle demons in games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1295267#post1295267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ugh, of course it did.<br /> <br /> Wasn't it <i>the point</i> with Erembour, that denizens of the Demon City could be subject to drastic change or remaking? I don't see those twisted by her music getting rounded up and purged.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That last bit you bolded might be hyperbole on Eldagusto part you know - not certain either way, just sayin... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aoi Cobalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1295586#post1295586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A human, yes.<br /> A 1st circle demon...? Only if there was a need for murderous florists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't say i agree on that. Demons can have individual desires, that may lead to formation of intimacies on their own like all other characters.<br /> Those can generate change or inspire a search for it on their own that might or not be consistent with their other desires. Not all change has to be imposed/external.<br /> <br /> Gervesin killed <b>craploads </b>of people across Creation for eras, before obliterating that one person whose doomed love for its city so fascinated Gervesin upon consumption that it deeply touche him and he fell in love with the being he destroyed. A fluke of fate, true, but far from a change imposed by another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 04-17-2019, 09:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T06:31:51-07:00","id":1305455,"title":"","content":"Can a human change? Yes. Is it difficult? Yes.<br /> <br /> Can a (non-asexual) human deny their sexual urges and live a life of celibacy? It's very difficult, but there are people who've done it. It's not really how we've evolved, but it's possible. They will still have the urge to act a certain way, but it can be resisted. Of course, some people are better at this than others.<br /> <br /> Can a human deny their urge to eat and drink? No, that'd kill them. But it's possible to restrict your urge, in fact most people do. Some are better or worse at it.<br /> <br /> Can a human deny their urge to socialise? Live an entirely solo life? Again, very difficult, but some people have gone off to live as solo hermits, etc.<br /> <br /> Can an Agatae restrict their jealousy of other steeds? Can a spider-demon put up with the barking of dogs? Can a Neomah not collect samples of organic matter to babies? Can a Blood Ape be a pacifist?<br /> These are all possible, but very difficult. Most demons are just not going to want to, and even if they did, most will fail. Humans can barely manage to be pacifists, let alone Blood Apes.<br /> <br /> <br /> We actually debated this in our last session. We're having a Conclave of the Cult of the Illuminated, and one member of the local Cult is Mara, the Shadow-Lover, who was converted by the Lunar social character in the party. So the question was whether it's possible for a Demon to genuinely convert to the Cult of the Illuminated, or whether they'll always be untrustworthy. Experts on demonology (like the Zenith and Eclipse solar-sorcerer) were consulted, and it was decided in the end that while most demons were fundamentally unhuman (there was a debate about whether the alien nature of demons is evil, or just different) and so would seem evil to humans, not all demons were definitely evil.<br /> <br /> <br /> Of course, this is my opinion, but I think the redeemability of demons is something that can be altered to your table. I know people have mentioned Jenna Moran quotes, but I think 3rd ed has moved away from these hard-and-fast rules about &quot;heroism&quot; as a hard-baked quality.<br /> <br /> I'll also point out that the line has always had Primordials and Devas that switched sides to the Incarnae; Gaia and Autocthon of course, but later there was stuff like the Deva who became one of the Gods in Luna's court.<br /> <br /> And one last thing; while first-circle demons are in some sense bred for a purpose, they're living beings, not robots. They're not absolutely programmed, they're not perfect automotons for the will of their creators (who are not, after all, all-powerful).<br /> Except Baidaks, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T07:08:25-07:00","id":1305461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1305455#post1305455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can a human deny their urge to eat and drink? No, that'd kill them.</div> </div> </div> </div>You say that as if it wouldn't be the point.<br /> <br /> I rather recall ten men in Maze prison who successfully denied the urge to eat and drink. I believe that one of them was a member of parliament.<br /> <br /> There are also the reports of Buddhist monks who spend years gradually reducing their intake of food and water for the sake of ensuring that their corpses when they finally starve themselves to death will be effectively mummified.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can an Agatae restrict their jealousy of other steeds? Can a spider-demon put up with the barking of dogs? Can a Neomah not collect samples of organic matter to babies? Can a Blood Ape be a pacifist?<br /> These are all possible, but very difficult. Most demons are just not going to want to, and even if they did, most will fail.</div> </div> </div> </div>The notion of a blood ape with an innate or instilled aversion to violence puts me in mind of Bruce from Finding Nemo; one could commit to it, but it's really important to avoid exposure to relapse triggers, and having a support system probably helps a lot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Humans can barely manage to be pacifists</div> </div> </div> </div>What, all of them?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T07:36:16-07:00","id":1305468,"title":"","content":"No, but that's my point.<br /> Humans can barely manage to be pacifists... but some have. Throughout history, it's estimated that there's been about 107,000,000,000 people. Even with a small chance of managing it, even with it being so difficult, of course there are people who've managed it because there have been so many humans.<br /> <br /> It may be very difficult for a demon to withstand the urges of that species (and while you're right about doing so in a way that might kill them, such as hunger strikes, I think that's not really generally the point of this discussion, since a demon that kills itself is no longer an NPC; though it is a good point).<br /> <br /> But it's not utterly impossible. If the ST wants to have a single pacifist Blood Ape or celibate Neomah, it's not canon-breaking.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The notion of a blood ape with an innate or instilled aversion to violence puts me in mind of Bruce from Finding Nemo; one could commit to it, but it's really important to avoid exposure to relapse triggers, and having a support system probably helps a lot. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that works. I find it much easier to restrict my urge to snack if I only have unappealing food in my fridge.<br /> Similarly, it probably helps Mara, in our game, to stay part of the Cult of the Illuminated because she hangs out with Shining Ones, who are mostly nice to her. If she was back in Malfeas, it would be much harder to keep her new faith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T09:25:51-07:00","id":1305495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1305468#post1305468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Humans can barely manage to be pacifists... but some have.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's kind of a truncated way of phrasing it; by those standards, 'humans' barely manage to be anything at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T09:31:52-07:00","id":1305499,"title":"","content":"Okay, to rephrase it; humans have various instincts and urges. It is very difficult to completely resist these instincts and urges, but it is possible. Most people are able to resist them to some extent when it would cause them problems (for example, people can resist their hunger pangs when they're worried about getting fat, or can't afford enough food but believe that solving this issue via crime, etc, would be worse than the hunger pangs). Only a few people can resist them entirely, but such people do exist.<br /> <br /> So I'd think all the same things would apply to demons. Most Teodozja can resist proselytising about the Yozis when necessary (for example, when a monk threatens to kill them if they keep doing it), but only a very small number can decide to live a life where they never proselytise about the Yozis. But such Teodozja do exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T12:59:19-07:00","id":1305536,"title":"","content":"I'm doubtful about that last. Aren't those particular demons a hive mind that would reinforce conformity of purpose among all their fellows by constant mental contact?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T14:42:06-07:00","id":1305563,"title":"","content":"The problem that I have is that I don't think demons can be meaningfully compared to humans.<br /> They are not some twisted, evil reflection of humans. They are alien creatures, who don't think like humans.<br /> I feel 2nd edition totally screwed this up with their write-up of Malfeas and the Infernals book. They changed demons from alien to twisted humans, who do the same sort of things (drink in bars, go to brothels, etc) that humans do (but with a twist, so it isn't quite the same).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24266-aoi-cobalt","name":"Aoi Cobalt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T15:55:47-07:00","id":1305584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aoi Cobalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1305563#post1305563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel 2nd edition totally screwed this up with their write-up of Malfeas and the Infernals book. They changed demons from alien to twisted humans, who do the same sort of things (drink in bars, go to brothels, etc) that humans do (but with a twist, so it isn't quite the same).</div> </div> </div> </div>I could point you to the parts of Games of Divinity that refer to demons going to bars and brothels, if you like.<br /> <br /> It's not even particularly difficult; it is, after all, integral to the write-ups of the sesseljae and neomah.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T15:55:56-07:00","id":1305585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aoi Cobalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1305563#post1305563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem that I have is that I don't think demons can be meaningfully compared to humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, but the facts are against you on this one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aoi Cobalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1305563#post1305563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are not some twisted, evil reflection of humans. They are alien creatures, who don't think like humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a binary switch, where not being the latter <i>must</i> make them the former.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aoi Cobalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1305563#post1305563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel 2nd edition totally screwed this up with their write-up of Malfeas and the Infernals book. They changed demons from alien to twisted humans, who do the same sort of things (<b>drink in bars, go to brothels</b>, etc) that humans do (but with a twist, so it isn't quite the same).</div> </div> </div> </div>The Demon City having taverns, wine-shops, and courtesans in it goes all the way back to <i>Games of Divinity.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-17-2019, 06:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T04:38:05-07:00","id":1305692,"title":"","content":"I admit I forgot that bit in <i>Games of Divinity</i>. But I also note that only citizens are allowed to patronize those places, which means the majority of first circle demons can not. Which limits the number of bars and brothels, and says something about the class of patron of such.<br /> <br /> All that aside, I guess I'm not liking the tendency to <i>humanize</i> demons. I'm having a hard time finding the words to put this into perspective for the rest of you readers of my posts.<br /> If I wanted outsiders to make twisted reflections of humans, there are Raksha. They do this job well. So do I really need to have demons do the same? Or can I keep them as alien creatures, who do what they do because it is what they do. <br /> I see demons as tools, say a chainsaw. A chainsaw isn't monstrous in itself, but what I can do with it can be monstrous. But the chainsaw itself doesn't care what it cuts, only that it is used to cut. <br /> <br /> I think that humans won the Primordial War because we could rise above ourselves and be heroes, and the Yozi couldn't. That the Yozi are locked into being themselves. And same with their souls, and their soul's souls, and those things they now create as tools (because if I'm stuck in hell because something someone made rebelled, I'm not going to allow any more of my creations that choice).<br /> <br /> I don't know if this babbling gets my point across, but can someone explain why they need demons to be the twisted human mockeries that they seem to be pushing for? Or have I read this idea wrong also?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24266-aoi-cobalt","name":"Aoi Cobalt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T04:46:36-07:00","id":1305693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aoi Cobalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1305692#post1305692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit I forgot that bit in <i>Games of Divinity</i>. But I also note that only citizens are allowed to patronize those places, which means the majority of first circle demons can not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't see that - mind providing a page number? Page 90 in fact even seems to directly contradict you. <br /> <br /> EDIT: Sorry, it is in fact page 89 that contradicts you.<br /> <br /> Also, just because they're people in a manner similar to the way humans are people doesn't mean they're a mockery of humans, intentional or otherwise. Please stop mischaracterizing our arguments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-18-2019, 08:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T05:07:21-07:00","id":1305696,"title":"","content":"Page 89.<br /> <br /> Also, are demons people in a manner similar to the way humans are people? I think you may have touched on the point of my disagreement with you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24266-aoi-cobalt","name":"Aoi Cobalt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T05:10:48-07:00","id":1305698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aoi Cobalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1305692#post1305692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also note that only citizens are allowed to patronize those places, which means the majority of first circle demons can not. Which limits the number of bars and brothels, and says something about the class of patron of such.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>page 89</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">a serf may have significant free time, which it spends loitering, carousing, resting, copulating, playing humane or monstrous games or \u2014 if it has its citizen\u2019s favor \u2014 drinking, dancing and telling stories in the wine shops of the city. Serfs of this sort may claim a home or even a mansion simply by moving in and defending it from rivals; the city has no shortage of real estate. Small groups of serfs often share a large building so that some can defend their few possessions while others go to do their lord\u2019s work.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aoi Cobalt</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">All that aside, I guess I'm not liking the tendency to <i>humanize</i> demons. I'm having a hard time finding the words to put this into perspective for the rest of you readers of my posts.<br /> If I wanted outsiders to make twisted reflections of humans, there are Raksha. They do this job well. So do I really need to have demons do the same? Or can I keep them as alien creatures, who do what they do because it is what they do.<br /> I see demons as tools, say a chainsaw. A chainsaw isn't monstrous in itself, but what I can do with it can be monstrous. But the chainsaw itself doesn't care what it cuts, only that it is used to cut.</div> </div> </div> </div>Demons in a thousand varieties crowd around. Some have comprehensible business, and others do not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aoi Cobalt</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that humans won the Primordial War because we could rise above ourselves and be heroes, and the Yozi couldn't. That the Yozi are locked into being themselves. And same with their souls, and their soul's souls, and those things they now create as tools</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a line that has kind of floated around the game in a few spots, and I find it unsatisfying. I think it's getting into characterization for the inhabitants of Malfeas that are somewhere between unnecessary and counterproductive, and kind of detracts from the victory of the Exalted to say that they won because of a deficiency of their enemies rather than because they managed to make war better.<br /> <br /> What does being a hero mean in this context? Does not being one mean that you can't surmount the Omphalos and perform some great rite up there? Does it mean you can't cast aside your nature as a scholar and become the Whim-of-the-Wind? Does it mean you can't conquer a full quarter of a layer of the Demon City, and turn your eyes to expansion in Creation?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aoi Cobalt</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">can someone explain why they need demons to be the twisted human mockeries that they seem to be pushing for?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think your characterization of going to a pub as twisted human mockeries is reductive, and I don't know what you mean by them being alien that would be presented in play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T05:50:11-07:00","id":1305706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does being a hero mean in this context?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why I don't like the older editions focus on beings being &quot;heroic&quot; or &quot;unheroic&quot;. It just isn't very clear what that means in practice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T06:06:34-07:00","id":1305711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1305698#post1305698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a line that has kind of floated around the game in a few spots, and I find it unsatisfying. I think it's getting into characterization for the inhabitants of Malfeas that are somewhere between unnecessary and counterproductive, and kind of detracts from the victory of the Exalted to say that they won because of a deficiency of their enemies rather than because they managed to make war better.<br /> <br /> What does being a hero mean in this context? Does not being one mean that you can't surmount the Omphalos and perform some great rite up there? Does it mean you can't cast aside your nature as a scholar and become the Whim-of-the-Wind? Does it mean you can't conquer a full quarter of a layer of the Demon City, and turn your eyes to expansion in Creation?</div> </div> </div> </div>And I feel that saying we won because we were better fighters detracts from the story for me.<br /> What does being a hero in this context mean? Maybe it isn't ambition, but sacrificing yourself to better the world. Maybe the Yozi can't (or don't want to be) be self-sacrificing. Maybe the war was not a forgone conclusion of better warrior exalts beating the Yozi, but a near run thing where the fact the Yozi could have won, but it would have asked them to be self-sacrificing, and the strong possibility of death caused Malfeas to surrender instead of fighting on. <br /> Yes, the enemy had a flaw, but the outcome wasn't cut and dried, and their power was above ours. I don't think that detracts from the story at all. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1305698#post1305698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think your characterization of going to a pub as twisted human mockeries is reductive, and I don't know what you mean by them being alien that would be presented in play.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's take neomah as an example. They exist to be courtesans. That was what they were made for. A few can have other interests, but its usually some form of art that they get passionate about.<br /> Do they get together at the end of the day, head to the bar for drinks and conversation like humans would? Or are they so caught up in what they are that doing that would be incomprehensible to them? <br /> <br /> Are they alien, as biological machines programmed to follow their passions, but utterly disinterested in anything else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24266-aoi-cobalt","name":"Aoi Cobalt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T06:16:51-07:00","id":1305714,"title":"","content":"This isn't precisely what you two are discussing, but I'd just like to point out that you can be alien without being a biological machine utterly disinterested in anything beyond your programming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T06:29:03-07:00","id":1305717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1305714#post1305714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn't precisely what you two are discussing, but I'd just like to point out that you can be alien without being a biological machine utterly disinterested in anything beyond your programming.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please, tell me more. I'm just spitballing here, other examples of alien behavior would be helpful, at least to me. I'm groping for concepts, maybe your are better than mine (and probably are).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24266-aoi-cobalt","name":"Aoi Cobalt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T08:44:33-07:00","id":1305734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aoi Cobalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1305711#post1305711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And I feel that saying we won because we were better fighters detracts from the story for me.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know about you, but I've never won a thing in my life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T10:19:11-07:00","id":1305751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1305734#post1305734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know about you, but I've never won a thing in my life.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, make fun of my adding us to the games definition of humanity. That really answers my question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24266-aoi-cobalt","name":"Aoi Cobalt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T10:44:23-07:00","id":1305761,"title":"","content":"It just makes it hard to take the conversation seriously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T11:12:10-07:00","id":1305767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1305761#post1305761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It just makes it hard to take the conversation seriously.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry. I will try to moderate myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24266-aoi-cobalt","name":"Aoi Cobalt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T11:24:32-07:00","id":1305769,"title":"","content":"All right, going over the examples in Games of Divinity and sorting into rough categories as I see them.<br /> <br /> The agata, angyalka, chrysogona, decanthrope, gilmyne, metody, neomah, perronele, tomescu: these ones strike me as the kind capable of the most complex personalities. They all have a particular remit, and favour certain moods and impulses that follow those, but I'd say they're capable of greater personal variations and recognitions of self and others. They can have wants, aspirations, preferences, particular relationships and personalised histories. The manner of what they are often makes these things strange; I think you'd be hard-pressed to call the likes of the agata, perronele and tomescu just twisted humans, in the oddities of their bodies and how they seek to live their lives.<br /> <br /> The luminata and teodozji are about as intelligent, but stranger. The deer who hunts men has a calculating malice, a focus and impulse towards tormenting other beings in their milieu, and the jade lions have a fanatical devotion to the Yozis.<br /> <br /> The amphelisia, passion moray and sesselja are basically higher order animals. I'd expect them to have about as much personality as a dog, which can be more than you'd expect, but still less than a human. Their needs are simple, but still focused on some particularly odd interactions with the world and ways of sustaining themselves.<br /> <br /> The firmin are a step below that, more on the order of an insect in terms of the sophistication of their reasoning and behaviour.<br /> <br /> And last is the hopping puppeteer, which is just plain weird. It's hardly even an animal, more of a bundle of nerves; it's all restlessness and roaming probing limbs. It builds things, but there's hardly any real intent there, it just flails around against the raw materials and leaves a construction or landscape behind.<br /> <br /> I'd say that's a reasonable cross-section of types they can have.<br /> <br /> The first category strike me as being possible to win over to new modes of thinking or ideals to live by or methods to apply their skills to. Some of them will be conveyed new, sometimes they're based on finding a way to align their own strange needs to the benefit of the Exalted or Heaven (I see the tomescu's desire to serve the will of immortals as something that could be won over). More than that, they're liable to want to find ways to be paid in kind for services to others.<br /> <br /> The animalistic ones might be trained, although they'll have impulses that need to be managed cautiously. The best trained dogs can still sometimes get over-excited and go a bit ballistic, the teakettle courtier is probably a bit harder to keep calm and more dangerous when it's pushed over the edge.<br /> <br /> The hopping puppeteer is basically mindless, there's nothing there to work with. Keep its energy focused on building things useful to you, and keep it directed away from people you don't want around it.<br /> <br /> And ones like the luminata and tedozji, I see hardly any recourse for, they're too nasty.<br /> <br /> {Before I reread the write-up in Games, I had a recollection of amphlisiae as more focused on collection of secrets, and thus designated it as one with a singular obsession and strange reactions in moods. I would have imagined that with the deer and lion}<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aoi Cobalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1305711#post1305711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Do they get together at the end of the day, head to the bar for drinks and conversation like humans would? </span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> Ah, I knew I forgot something. This kind of behaviour, socialising, sharing stories, communicating news and gossip, I'd see this as the kind of things that the first group would do.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 04-18-2019, 02:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T11:44:34-07:00","id":1305773,"title":"","content":"I would suggest that all demons are dangerous, much like all humans are dangerous, though the reason they are dangerous will vary from species to species (or individual to individual for Third and Second Circle demons). A neomah may be dangerous because 'she' steals the heart of your child, because 'she' allows your infertile relative to have a child who deprives you of an inheritance, or because 'she' produces a demon-human-scorpian-lion child that reproduces by impregnating virgin human girls with its song. In any case, the danger exists, the question is whether it can be mitigated through negotiation or just prevented through superior force.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25244-the-fool-of-creation","name":"The Fool of Creation","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T20:15:12-07:00","id":1305887,"title":"","content":"Wait.<br /> <br /> Neomah are courtesans? I thought they were breeding vats","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T20:50:01-07:00","id":1305894,"title":"","content":"They are great because they can be both <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. On a more serious note though, neomah are probably one of the most dangerous demons because they are eager to give people what they want, and they only want to have a chance to reproduce. Of course, their children might give nightmares to Yozis, but it is not like the neomah usually care about their fate after they are born.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25244-the-fool-of-creation","name":"The Fool of Creation","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T20:56:55-07:00","id":1305895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1294000-demons-must-they-be-dangerous?p=1305887#post1305887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neomah are courtesans? I thought they were breeding vats</div> </div> </div> </div>To summarise the core: Neomah weave nautilus towers in which ply their trade as shape-shifting courtesans in return for a small part of their clients' substance, which they use to craft infants in the fires of their towers, which they then abandon. The infants, that is. The towers are dismantled before moving on to new pastures. <br /> <br /> Sometimes they are summoned specifically to craft an infant, but they'll do it unasked if they have the opportunity. As such, while they may also be summoned to become spies or bodyguards, this does not preclude them following their nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 04-18-2019, 11:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}